The orbital map changes to a subsurface cross-section. The evaluator points to the layers where orbital data suggests ice may be present. Salts complicate the radar reading here. On Mars, extremely cold ice also makes drilling harder and can sublimate when exposed. At the same speed, Siloli wind exerts more force on a panel because the air is denser. You will run three tests: detect a buried target, extract a frozen core, and mount panels against the gusts. On the surface, use the field ultraviolet protection.
